{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RedBlackTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lookup, insertion and removal take O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"), and the height stays at most 2 log₂("},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" + 1)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"An insertion rotates at most twice and a removal at most three times; the recolouring above"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them is O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") in the worst case and O(1) amortized."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The elements are a random-access collection in ascending order, indexed by rank like an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array: "},{"code":"tree[0]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the smallest element. Reading an element by index costs O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"), and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass through the whole collection costs O("},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var primes: RedBlackTree = [7, 2, 11, 3, 5]","primes.insert(13)","primes.contains(4)        \/\/ false","Array(primes)             \/\/ [2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13]","primes.lowerBound(6)      \/\/ 3, the index of 7"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"type":"text","text":" links, so the tree holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees"]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A sorted set kept in a red–black tree: a binary search tree whose vertices are red or black,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with no red vertex under a red one and the same number of black vertices on every path from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"root down (Guibas and Sedgewick, 1978)."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Se","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SE","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SH","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/ST","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s10SetAlgebraP"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap"],"anchor":"Sorted-sets","title":